  "content": {
    "id": "v2-p31-practice-slot-7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^{2}\\frac{x^2+4}{x}\\,dx$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Undefined.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\int_{-1}^{2}\\frac{x^2+4}{x}\\,dx&=\\int_{-1}^{2}\\left(x+\\frac4x\\right)dx\\end{align*}$$\nThe term $\\dfrac4x$ is undefined at $x=0$, which lies inside $[-1,2]$. The improper integrals on either side of $0$ do not converge, so the definite integral is undefined.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
